{
  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "The current best (config_041: pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.635) establishes that a simple PCA RNA encoder combined with a strong image encoder and avgpool aggregation is highly effective. The most impactful remaining design question is whether a learned RNA representation (scvi_n200) can outperform PCA in this same setting. config_049 changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while keeping imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, and weighted fusion fixed, directly testing whether a biologically informed learned embedding adds value over the linear PCA baseline. This is the best use of the next slot because it (1) exploits the strongest configuration found so far, (2) reduces uncertainty on the RNA encoder axis—a major source of variance across experiments—and (3) if it improves, opens a new exploitation path for the remaining 3 experiments; if it does not, it confirms pca_n2000 as optimal and lets us focus remaining budget on fusion or other micro-variations around the known best."
}

